      "id": 59178,
      "name": "Drakossozh",
      "username": "Drakossozh",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/f05b48/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-08T17:33:27.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>celette, if it helps, this is what I did for AA (He is the hero I had the hardest time figuring out.) I laid out all of his cards in front of me, and started to just try to chain everything together. I looked at what the cards did, and then I looked at what instruments would let me use those cards. With everything laid out in front of me as if in a real game, it wasn't that hard. And then I played a \"practice\" game, no villain, no other heroes, no environment, just AA. I'd run through a few turns, get a feel for him. And then I'd get good ole' BB, Gloomy, or the Rat (my default punching bag Villains), then I'd pic some of my favorite heroes (so they could cover for AA if he messed up) then just...played. Got it on my second run through with a villain, while when I did it for NM and AZ, I got it on the first. So yey!</p>",
